# Bitwarden CLI local state — NEVER commit.
# storage/path.rs resolves appdata to ./bw-data when it exists, so running the
# binary from the repo root drops state here. `data.json` holds legacy tokens;
# `user.sqlite` now holds the live access and refresh tokens
# (`authentication_tokens`), the API-key client secret when one is used
# (`user_login_method`), and the session-sealed user key
# (`session_protected_user_key`). The .sqlite patterns are listed separately from
# bw-data/ on purpose: BITWARDENCLI_APPDATA_DIR can put them anywhere.
bw-data/
data.json
user.sqlite
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
__PROTECTED__*
*.bwsession
